ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "3.0.3", text = "A NEW tag now points out recently added options.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Settings: new options show a |cffffffffNEW|r tag, and so do their tab and page. Once you've opened a page and moved on, its tags are gone for good. New installs don't get them.\n• Options > AddOns: FlareUI's row shows a |cffffffffNEW|r tag while any of its pages still has one. Not in the Gamepad UI.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffButton art|r is now |cffffffffShow button art|r.\n• Quest Tracker: |cffffffffCollapse completed quests|r is now |cffffffffCollapse completed|r." },
    { version = "3.0.2", text = "Better proc glows on your action bars.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Proc Glow: |cffffffffVictory Rush|r now glows while you can use it, and goes dark during its cooldown.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Proc Glow: Revenge goes dark after you use it, instead of staying lit for the rest of its window. It comes back when you next block, dodge or parry. Blizzard can hide your casts in dungeons and raids, so there it may stay lit as before.\n• Proc Glow: a glow should no longer flicker or go out when you press another ability during the global cooldown.\n• Proc Glow: procs already active when you reload now glow right away, and a glow that got stuck clears the next time you change zones.\n• Proc Glow: reaction abilities are now checked by class, so a spell with the same name on another class no longer glows by mistake.\n• Performance: Proc Glow does less work on classes with no reaction abilities." },
    { version = "3.0.1", text = "Simpler action bar paging, class colours for each frame, and more ways to read your XP.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Unit frames: |cffffffffClass Colours|r is now in each frame's Edit Mode dialog, under Look, on the player, target, focus, target of target, target of focus, party and raid frames. It's on by default. If you had the old option off, every frame starts off. The Resource Bars' health bar follows the player frame.\n• XP bar: |cffffffffXP Bar Numbers|r in the Action Bars settings shows current / max, a percentage, both, or what's left to go. Reputation and honor use it too.\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffNo Auto-Paging for Stances|r keeps a warrior's Action Bar 1 on its page when changing stance. It's off by default, but stays on if you'd already stopped stance paging in 3.0.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffAllow Auto-paging|r is now one toggle, |cffffffffAuto-Paging for Stealth|r, for rogues. Druid forms and warrior stances are back to Blizzard's own paging, and bars 2 to 8 no longer page. If you'd set it to No Auto-Paging, the new toggle starts off.\n• Quest Tracker: shift-click now tracks and untracks quests. Ctrl-click sets the focus.\n• Unit Frames settings: |cffffffffClass colours|r moved to Edit Mode.\n• Action Bars settings: |cffffffffFade Options|r is gone from the page. Fading is still in each bar's Edit Mode dialog.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Action Bars: reports of druid form paging not working since 3.0 should be fixed by the paging change above." },
    { version = "3.0", text = "Portrait versions of your target of target and focus target frames, smooth bars, a much better Quest Tracker, and animations where they count. This one's big, so here's the lot.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Unit frames: |cffffffffTarget of Target|r and |cffffffffTarget of Focus|r now have small portrait versions in FlareUI and Forever Style, like the pet. |cffffffffSimple \"Target Of\"|r in the Unit Frames settings keeps the plain frames, and the two keep separate settings and positions.\n• Unit frames, Resource Bars: |cffffffffSmooth Bar Animations|r in Edit Mode makes health and power glide to their new value. It's off by default, and sits under Background Opacity on every frame that has it. Target of Target and Target of Focus don't have it.\n• Pet frames: |cffffffffAuras|r and |cffffffffAura Ordering|r in Edit Mode, in every style. Buffs and Debuffs are off by default.\n• Target, focus and boss frames: |cffffffffHide Buffs|r in Edit Mode, set to Permanent by default, which is how they already behaved.\n• Resource Bars: |cffffffffBackground Opacity|r in Edit Mode.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: |cffffffffArrival animation|r fades new icons in as they drop into place. It's off by default.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: opening the settings page shows sample icons, so you can see your Timer, Icon Shape and Swipe choices as you change them.\n• Quest Tracker: quests slide in when accepted and out when turned in, the rest make room, and a finished objective gets a soft sheen.\n• Quest Tracker: timed quests show a countdown that goes from green to yellow, orange and red, even on a collapsed quest, and they stay listed when you leave their zone.\n• Quest Tracker: completed quests show their own text, like where to turn them in. Auto-complete quests finish when you click them.\n• Quest Tracker: scenario objectives show above your quests, a line shows the gold a quest still needs, and your focused quest shows its next waypoint when the game gives one.\n• Quest Tracker: new options in the settings:\n      - |cffffffffCollapse completed quests|r\n      - |cffffffffHide finished objectives|r\n      - |cffffffffHide quest level|r\n      - |cffffffffFocus buttons|r\n      - |cffffffffVoice buttons|r, with the Spoken addon\n• Quest Tracker: |cffffffffBy progress|r in Objective Sorting, and |cffffffffQuest Spacing|r in Edit Mode.\n• Quest Tracker: |cffffffffShow on Map|r and |cffffffffLink to Chat|r in the right-click menu, and shift-click a zone heading to fold all its quests.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Forever Style: |cffffffffBackground Opacity|r is gone from unit, party and boss frames. The frame's own art is the background there, and the slider only painted over it.\n• Forever Style: Target of Target and Target of Focus use smaller text.\n• Action Bars, Unit Frames: the banner pointing to Edit Mode is shorter and harder to miss.\n• Buffs: the default position moved down by one pixel. Only frames you haven't moved follow it.\n• Fake Cooldown Manager: the setup button and its right-click hint only show as available when a bar uses it.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffNo Auto-Paging|r now really stops Action Bar 1 changing page with a warrior's stance. Picking another bar for Auto-Paging does the same.\n• Quest Tracker: quest levels use the same colours as the quest log.\n• Quest Tracker: failed quests now say so.\n• Quest Tracker: opening a quest from the tracker in combat or in the Gamepad UI is now refused with a message. It could cause errors or break controller bindings.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: sample timers now show in Edit Mode.\n• Party, raid and boss frames: possible errors from hidden names in instances.\n• Quality of Life: Sync Blizz UI could fail to save your chat windows.\n• The prompt to reload after copying interface settings now tells you how if you answer it in combat.\n• Performance: less work in raids, mainly on party and raid frames, roster changes, threat on hidden frames, swing timers, and big guilds with Level Before Names on.\n• A smaller download." },
    { version = "2.10.0", text = "A setup tour for new players, and a mana bar for druids in Bear and Cat Form.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• A |cffffffffsetup tour|r now greets new players. It shows what each part of FlareUI does, lets you turn each one on and pick your unit frame style, and explains where the options live. Nothing changes until you click |cffffffffReload and finish|r on the last page, and you can skip it from the first page.\n• About: a |cffffffffStart Tour|r button runs the tour again, and so does |cffffd100/fui tour|r.\n• Player frame: |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r in Edit Mode shows a thin mana bar under the power bar when a druid is in a form that doesn't use mana. It's off by default, and isn't available in Forever Style.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Chat: voice chat's \"who's speaking\" names no longer sit on top of the mute buttons or flash to the left when someone stops talking. They stay above the chat's left edge. Other alerts that share that spot follow the same stack." },
}
